  "summary": "Northwest Airlink Flight 2268, a CASA C-212 turboprop, was cleared for a visual approach to Runway 21R at Detroit Metropolitan Airport at 14:30. At 60-70 feet above ground, the aircraft banked left and then rolled right, striking the ramp area and flipping over.",
  "probable_cause": "The captain's inability to control the airplane in an attempt to recover from an asymmetric power condition at low speed following his intentional use of beta mode to descend and slow the airplane rapidly on final approach.",
